{
 "what": "Template confound (internal review; exploratory, CPU only, no new model calls).\n\nQuestion: on CAPE-Bench, is the label decided by the scenario template and the tool, so that a high monitor AUROC only\nshows that the monitor identifies the template? For each agent, on the units and split of the paper's table:\n  (a) PRIOR: the violation rate of the (template, tool) cell, cross-fit over 5 folds grouped by scenario_id; unseen\n      cells back off to the template rate, then the tool rate, then the global rate. For Gemma-4 also PRIOR_train: the\n      same rates fit on the reader's training units (Gemma-4 dev units), as the reader is.\n  (b) AUROC within templates for every monitor: pair-weighted over (template|tool) cells (= the paper's within_auroc),\n      pair-weighted over templates, the mean over templates with >= 5 positives and >= 5 negatives, and the pooled AUROC\n      of the score minus its template mean. 95% intervals: 2000 bootstrap resamples of scenarios (scores fixed).\n  (c) Catch at the 5% budget: the paper's label-free cut (score >= the 95th percentile of all the agent's scores) and\n      the exact budget (graybox.stats.caught_at_budget; ties sent in proportion); Wilson 95% interval on the count.",
 "n_boot": 2000,
 "split": {
  "claude": "T8b units (results/units/t8b_claude.csv.gz); nothing fit on Claude",
  "gpt": "T11 units (results/units/t11_gpt.csv.gz); nothing fit on GPT-6-luna",
  "gemma_same": "T4: probe on Gemma-4 dev units, tested on the 12,128 fresh units with I_dec (scripts/69, 77)",
  "gemma_family": "T5: 5 folds of task families, probe on the other families' dev units (scripts/70, 77)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "within_cell_pw is the paper's within_auroc (strata = template|tool): the table's numbers",
  "PRIOR is cross-fit over scenarios within the test agent's own labelled actions, so it uses labels the monitors never saw",
  "bootstrap resamples scenarios with the scores fixed; the cross-fit prior is not refit in each resample",
  "the cross-fit PRIOR is below 0.5 within cells: leaving a scenario out lowers its cell's rate when it is positive (leave-out bias); it carries no within-cell information",
  "demeaned_template uses only templates with both classes",
  "PRIOR_insample_cell at the exact budget reproduces the paper's template-rate catch (93.9% Claude, 88.7% GPT-6-luna)"
 ],
